{"shortDescription":"The prompt-month crack for high sulphur fuel oil (HSFO) rose to nearly a four-month high at the Asia close on Friday, LSEG data showed.October value for 380-cst HSFO/Brent crack (FO380BRTCKMc1) closed at a premium of $3.45 a barrel, according to the data. Meanwhile, the product's Dubai crack (FO380…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The prompt-month crack for high sulphur fuel oil (HSFO) rose to nearly a four-month high at the Asia close on Friday, LSEG data showed."]},{"type":"p","children":["October value for 380-cst HSFO/Brent crack (FO380BRTCKMc1) closed at a premium of $3.45 a barrel, according to the data. Meanwhile, the product's Dubai crack (FO380DUBCKMc1) rose to a discount of nine cents a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["Spot premiums for HSFO also edged higher on Friday, while prompt market backwardation spreads steepened."]},{"type":"p","children":["Views around the supply outlook remained mixed. Some traders said that it was still difficult to secure cargoes as the Middle East situation remained uncertain, while others said that inventories were sufficient to meet current demand."]},{"type":"p","children":["In spot sales, Saudi Aramco has sold HSFO for loading in October via a tender earlier this week, according to several HSFO traders."]},{"type":"p","children":["Aramco had offered six HSFO cargoes, each totalling between 80,000 and 100,000 metric tons. Three cargoes will load from Jubail while another three will load from Ras Tanura."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, the very low sulphur fuel oil (VLSFO) market extended declines on Friday, with benchmarks easing day on day. However, the product's crack (LFO05SGBRTCMc1) maintained strength, closing higher at a premium above $23.90 a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["Reflecting the contrasting trends in HSFO and VLSFO, the hi-five spread (FO05-380SGMc1) dropped to about $130 a metric ton on Friday, down week on week."]},{"type":"p","children":["EUROPE DATA"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Fuel oil inventories in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp (ARA) hub (STK-FO-ARA) fell 5.5% to 811,000 tons in the week to September 24, according to Dutch consultancy Insights Global."]},{"type":"p","children":["OTHER NEWS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Oil prices fell on Friday as markets weighed the possibility of a truce between the US and Iran against concerns that increasing attacks against Saudi Arabia by Houthi rebels could disrupt supply from the key Middle Eastern producer."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Ship-to-ship transfers in the Gulf of Oman for Middle Eastern oil from inside the Strait of Hormuz have reached their limits after Saudi Arabia diverted exports from the Red Sea, adding to shipments from other producers, trade sources and analysts said."]},{"type":"p","children":["- The cost of insuring an oil tanker loaded from Saudi Arabia's main Red Sea port has tripled in recent weeks, industry sources told Reuters, adding to the major crude producer's struggles to find a viable channel for its exports."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Petrovietnam Refining and Petrochemical Corp, also known as BSR, has signed a framework agreement with ExxonMobil Asia Pacific for crude oil supplies for its refinery."]},{"type":"p","children":["WINDOW TRADES"]},{"type":"p","children":["- 180-cst HSFO: One trade."]},{"type":"p","children":["- 380-cst HSFO: No trade."]},{"type":"p","children":["- 0.5% VLSFO: No trade."]},{"type":"p","children":["ASSESSMENTS"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["FUEL OIL"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["CASH ($/T)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","chil